From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:43:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nb/intel/haswell/native_raminit: Wait longer for a Vref move
 that is late

update_vref_and_wait() waits 50 us for the done bit of the Vref circuit
and warns if it has not come. Most moves are done by then, the steps
of one of the training scans and the moves of 8 of the command
training. A move of several steps is not always: the 2D centring moves
the write Vref of a channel by up to 18 steps between its points, and
on a ThinkPad W541 the circuit of channel 1 missed the 50 us three
times in one training, so that some margins of that channel may have
been measured at a reference still moving.

When the done bit has not come in 50 us, wait for it up to 10 ms, as
set_dimm_vref() does for a long move, then 1 ms more for what is
between the circuit and the DIMMs; warn only if it does not come at
all. A move done in time costs nothing more.

TEST=Build of the ThinkPad W541 with the native RAM init.

Change-Id: I036b53fcb0e7e4abcea455bd6bb709948ea2cd3c
---
 .../haswell/native_raminit/change_margin.c    | 30 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/change_margin.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/change_margin.c
index 107e12769d..cf0aeb58c2 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/change_margin.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/change_margin.c
@@ -126,6 +126,11 @@ static uint32_t get_vref_done_bit(const enum dimm_vref_type vref_type)
 	}
 }
 
+/* For a move of more than one step: how long to wait for the circuit */
+#define DIMM_VREF_FAR_TIMEOUT_MS	10
+/* And then for what is between it and the DIMMs */
+#define DIMM_VREF_FAR_SETTLE_MS		1
+
 void update_vref_and_wait(
 	struct sysinfo *ctrl,
 	const enum dimm_vref_type vref_type,
@@ -158,7 +163,14 @@ void update_vref_and_wait(
 	}
 	mchbar_write32(vref_reg, ddr_vref_adjust.raw);
 
-	/* Wait for Vref to settle (note: CA Vref takes longer to settle) */
+	/*
+	 * Wait for Vref to settle (note: CA Vref takes longer to settle). Most
+	 * moves are done within 50 us. One that is not, a move of several steps
+	 * (the 2D centring moves the write Vref by up to 18), gets more time, and
+	 * then as long again for what is between the circuit and the DIMMs, as
+	 * set_dimm_vref() gives a long move; the moves that were done in time
+	 * cost nothing more.
+	 */
 	if (!skip_wait) {
 		struct stopwatch timer;
 		stopwatch_init_usecs_expire(&timer, 50);
@@ -166,15 +178,19 @@ void update_vref_and_wait(
 			if (mchbar_read32(vref_reg) & done_bit)
 				return;
 		} while (!stopwatch_expired(&timer));
-		printk(BIOS_WARNING, "Vref circuit %u failed to converge\n", vref_type);
+
+		stopwatch_init_msecs_expire(&timer, DIMM_VREF_FAR_TIMEOUT_MS);
+		while (!(mchbar_read32(vref_reg) & done_bit)) {
+			if (stopwatch_expired(&timer)) {
+				printk(BIOS_WARNING, "Vref circuit %u failed to converge\n",
+				       vref_type);
+				return;
+			}
+		}
+		mdelay(DIMM_VREF_FAR_SETTLE_MS);
 	}
 }
 
-/* For a move of more than one step: how long to wait for the circuit */
-#define DIMM_VREF_FAR_TIMEOUT_MS	10
-/* And then for what is between it and the DIMMs */
-#define DIMM_VREF_FAR_SETTLE_MS		1
-
 /*
  * Set a DIMM Vref to a value of its range, not to an offset from the saved
  * one, as a scan of the whole range needs; saved as the new value or not.
-- 
2.56.0

